    "created_at": "2023-02-01T09:11:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-02T10:54:37Z",
    "body": "> With the case of the `keys()` iterator here, would the intention of this PR be to make it so that `set-cookie` could appear multiple times? Or should the `keys()` iterator always only produce a unique set? The way this is currently defined, it would appear that the keys iterator could have `set-cookie` multiple times.\r\n\r\nThat seems intentional in the way pair iteration works in WebIDL. That way, `[...headers.keys()].length === [...headers.values()].length` and the indices match.\r\n\r\nDo you think this would break some existing code, though?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
